** Live adaptive refinement of a distributed model, with rebalancing that moves the children: each
** process creates only the elements it computes; at every topology check (every output increment)
** a field-output marker -- the axial stress, gathered from the processes -- refines the elements the
** stress wave from the pulled right end has reached. The children of a refined element are created
** by the process computing it, which transfers its state to them; refined and unrefined elements
** meet at hanging nodes. The model is then repartitioned with the element numbers as costs
** (load-balance-costs=elementNumber), which the new, high-numbered children dominate, so that
** children move between the processes (migration). A body force on every element makes each
** process create the loaded elements touching its own as well, also the children. The result is
** that of a serial run.

*material, name=LinearElastic, id=linearelastic
**E      nu   density
20000.0, 0.2, 2.0e-9

*section, name=section1, material=linearelastic, type=solid
gen_all

*job, name=nedAmrRebalanceJob, domain=3d

** courant-number=0.1: see NEDLiveAMR.
*solver, solver=NEDMPI, name=theSolver
courant-number=0.1
output-frequency=20
topology-check-frequency=20
load-balance-costs=elementNumber

*modelGenerator, generator=boxGen, name=gen
nX      =6
nY      =1
nZ      =1
lX      =60
lY      =10
lZ      =10
elType  =C3D20R

*modelModifier, type=hAdaptivity, name=amrLive
>>marker, type=fieldOutput, fieldOutput=sxx, operator='>=', threshold=0.15
refineElSet=gen_all
maxLevel=1

*fieldOutput
>>perElement, elSet=gen_all, name=sxx, result=stress, quadraturePoint=0:8, f(x)='np.max(np.abs(x[:,:,0]),axis=1)'
>>perNode, name=Ux, nSet=gen_right, field=displacement, result=U, f(x)='np.mean(x[:,0])', saveHistory=True
>>perNode, name=RF, nSet=gen_left, field=displacement, result=P, f(x)='np.sum(x[:,0])', saveHistory=True

*output, type=monitor, name=monitor
fieldOutput=RF

*step, type=adaptiveForExplicitSimulations, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1, minInc=1e-14, maxNumInc=120, maxIter=25, stepLength=1e-3
>>dirichlet, name=fixLeft,  nSet=gen_left,  field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=pullRight, nSet=gen_right, field=displacement, 1=0.05
>>bodyForce, name=gravity, elSet=gen_all, forceVector='0.0, -1e-6, 0.0', f(t)=t
